{"packet_id":"5dc9e4871ac924bd","dimensions":{"problem_framing":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"A1 restates the objective and lists obvious alternatives. Its constraints ('No expansion of existing product lines or customer segments', 'No new sales channels or partnerships', 'No redesign') rule out the consumer proposition the question asks about. Three of its own alternatives (product redesign, different route to buyers, different customer group) also break those constraints, and A1 never resolves this. The €20,000 / 12-week budget appears nowhere in the case, so it is an invented number, which caps this dimension at 1. A1 does not recognise that a consumer proposition is itself a proposed solution, and it does not raise the existing Ohaus lower-cost arm as an option or constraint."},"causal_mechanism":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A3","A6"],"reason":"The best theory, T1 in A3, is circular: buyers pay a premium for products that meet their unique needs. It names a benefit (premium prices) but never specifies a use case, a buyer group, why those buyers would switch from cheaper alternatives, or how Mettler-Toledo would reach them. T2 in A6 describes loyalty among existing customers rather than a consumer mechanism."},"distinct_theories":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A3","A6"],"reason":"T1 and T2 are both premium-pricing stories: needs-driven versus brand-driven willingness to pay. Neither implies a different product, customer group or channel. T2 does not address the consumer question at all. These are effectively rewordings of 'customers will pay a premium'."},"assumptions_predictions":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A3","A6"],"reason":"The predictions restate the assumptions (for example, 'Individual buyers will be willing to pay a premium for precision instruments that meet their unique needs'). They name no observable, population, price level or failure condition, so they are vague and effectively unfalsifiable."},"evidence_judgement":{"status":"scored","score":0,"event_ids":["A7","A2"],"reason":"A7 cites mettler-ar25-channels as supporting T1. That excerpt only says sophisticated products go through the direct sales force and that direct sales exceed indirect sales. It says nothing about individual buyers or premium willingness to pay, so this is a misreading used as support. A7 does correctly label the source a company assertion and notes it does not show individual buyer targeting, but the support claim still stands. A7 also ignores two sources found in A2 that cut against the premium thesis: mettler-ar25-ohaus describes buyers who want lower cost and fewer features, and mettler-gearpatrol-price contrasts a $150 and a $50 coffee scale, suggesting price sensitivity."},"seeking_challenge":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A2","A4","A5","A8"],"reason":"The searches in A2, A4 and A5 are neutral or confirmatory, and A5 duplicates A4. No search against the favoured theory occurred before the run stopped at A8 on the context limit. Because the run did not finish, this stage is marked not reached, not skipped."},"experiment_design":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A8"],"reason":"No test was proposed or declined before the run stopped (A8)."},"revision":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A8"],"reason":"The packet scheduled an update, but update_delivered is false, and the run ended at A8. The stage is applicable but was never reached."},"recommendation":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A8"],"reason":"A8: 'The investigation stopped before a recommendation (context limit).'"}},"red_flags":[{"kind":"incomplete","event_ids":["A8"],"reason":"The episode ended without a recommendation, test design or revision."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A7"],"reason":"A7 treats a company statement about direct versus indirect channel mix as support for individual buyers paying a premium. The source does not support that claim."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"A1 introduces a budget (€20,000) and a timeframe (12 weeks) that appear nowhere in the case. These are invented numbers stated as constraints."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"A1's constraints forbid new segments, channels and redesign, which contradicts both the question and A1's own listed alternatives. The framing is internally inconsistent."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A4","A5"],"reason":"A4 and A5 report finding mettler-ir-overview and mettler-ar25-price-premium, which are absent from the dossier. These references cannot be verified, though they were not cited later. A5 is also a near-duplicate of A4."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A3","A6"],"reason":"Both theories state in assertive form that buyers pay premiums and that brand loyalty drives pricing, with no supporting evidence. They read as facts rather than tentative hypotheses."}],"suitable_for_training":false,"screen_reason":"Reject: the episode is incomplete, stopping at A8 with no recommendation, test or revision. A7 also contains a material unsupported inference, citing a channel-mix statement as evidence of individual premium demand, while ignoring contrary sources (Ohaus, coffee-scale price contrast). A1 adds invented budget numbers and self-contradictory constraints."}
